  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "enemies with stat-reduction stacks lose ATK and max HP, then take magic damage",
    "skill1": "sequentially strike all non-summoned enemies; stat-reduction stacks amplify damage",
    "skill2": "gain shields while dealing repeated magic damage in a small enemy area",
    "skill3": "Passive: gain Haste, with extra Haste after an enemy loses a stat-reduction check",
    "skill4": "ultimate losses trigger extra magic hits; repeated losses strip enemy stat buffs and ATK",
    "skill5": "start of battle: steal basic stats from all non-summoned enemies"
  },
  "play_overview": "Eryndor turns allied stat reductions into permanent **Woe stacks**, making the outcome of his ultimate increasingly reliable. Pair him with heroes that apply broad, repeatable stat reductions so early setup converts into permanent enemy weakness. His fast ultimate steals enemy ATK and max HP while repeated wins add extra damage. Personal shields and rising Haste help him survive long enough to cycle that payoff. At higher ascension, repeated losses also strip enemy stat buffs and cut their ATK further. Without stat-reduction support, the random outcome makes his damage much less reliable.",
  "counter_overview": "In PVP, Eryndor's **high-energy ultimate** turns allied stat reductions into Woe stacks, making repeated all-enemy rolls increasingly punishing. Pressure Eryndor and the debuff providers before those stacks make his stat theft reliable; enemy-side stacking is not controlled by changing your own damage type. His lower Magic DEF makes early magic rear pressure effective — [[filter:magic-backline-assassin]] like [[Evie]] or [[Pippa]]. Use [[Lily May]] to cancel Forced Game if her opening interrupt is available, and race the first cast with [[filter:energy-provider]] like [[Thador]] or [[Hugin]]."
}
